## Synthesis Optimization

Synthesis tools optimize RTL to generate efficient hardware while maintaining the required functionality.

### Topics Covered

- Logic optimization
- Technology-independent optimization
- Technology mapping
- Optimization of constant multiplications
- Multiplication by powers of two using shifts
- Multiplication by constants using simpler logic
- Bit-width and concatenation-based optimizations
- Reduction of unnecessary hardware
- Area, power and performance considerations

### Examples

- Multiplication by 8 can be implemented using a left shift.
- Multiplication by 9 can be implemented as `A × 8 + A`, which can be realized using shifting and addition.
- Some operations can be implemented through simple wiring/bit manipulation instead of standard-cell logic.

### Key Learning

RTL should be written with the resulting hardware in mind. Synthesis tools can recognize certain patterns and optimize them into simpler hardware, reducing unnecessary area, power and delay.
